      "source": [
        "1. grid_size=(6, 6): Defines the grid size, creating a 6x6 grid for displaying images.\n",
        "2. figsize=(12, 12): Specifies the size of the figure, making it large enough to clearly display all images.\n",
        "3. plt.subplot(grid_size[0], grid_size[1], i): Creates a subplot in the specified grid position.\n",
        "4. plt.suptitle(...): Adds a title above the entire grid to indicate whether the images are from the training or testing dataset."
      ]
